          "id": "image-text",
          "text": "OPERATIONAL SUMMARY\n(Unaudited)\nQ3-2025 Q4-2025 Q1-2026 Q2-2026 Q3-2026 YoY\nModel 3/Y production 435,826 422,652 394,611 442,936 457,387 5%\nOther models production 11,624 11,706 13,775 8,822 7,004 -40%\nTotal production(1) 447,450 434,358 408,386 451,758 464,391 4%\nModel 3/Y deliveries 481,166 406,585 341,893 467,762 478,237 -1%\nOther models deliveries 15,933 11,642 16,130 12,364 8,295 -48%\nTotal deliveries(1) 497,099 418,227 358,023 480,126 486,532 -2%\nof which subject to operating lease accounting 10,230 10,996 3,430 7,580 6,911 -32%\nCumulative deliveries(2) (all-time; mil) 8.5 8.9 9.2 9.7 10.2 20%\nActive FSD Subscriptions(3) (mil) 1.04 1.10 1.28 1.48 1.74 67%\nTotal end of quarter operating lease (new vehicle) count(4) 167,163 163,075 151,991 141,876 133,720 -20%\nGlobal vehicle inventory (days of supply)(5) 10 15 27 15 11 10%\nStorage deployed (GWh) 12.5 14.2 8.8 13.5 13.7 10%\nSupercharger stations 7,753 8,182 8,463 8,704 8,904 15%\nSupercharger connectors 73,817 77,682 79,918 82,357 84,465 14%\n(1) Vehicle production and delivery numbers represent passenger vehicles sold to customers.\n(2) In accordance with our 2025 CEO Performance Award, metric includes all new Tesla vehicles delivered to customers plus any unsupervised Robotaxis placed into commercial operation. For further detail see our 2025 Proxy Statement.\n(3) In accordance with our 2025 CEO Performance Award, metric includes both upfront payment and monthly subscriptions and excludes free trials. For further detail see our 2025 Proxy Statement.\n(4) Beginning in Q4'25, end of quarter operating lease count pertains only to new vehicles. Q3'25 has been adjusted to exclude used vehicles.\n5 (5) Days of supply is calculated by dividing new vehicle ending inventory by the relevant quarter's deliveries and using 75 trading days (aligned with Automotive News definition).\nT E S L A",
